WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.055 --> 00:00:08.986
Scrooge was still trying to recover from his shock about Tiny Tim when Bob Cratchit arrived home.

2
00:00:08.987 --> 00:00:14.320
The man's cheeks were red from the cold, and he was huddled into a thick scarf.

3
00:00:14.321 --> 00:00:18.438
Belinda rushed to bring her father a hot cup of tea.

4
00:00:18.439 --> 00:00:26.003
Peter hung up Bob's coat while the younger two children folded the scarf and put it away.

5
00:00:26.004 --> 00:00:31.758
Once their father was settled by the fire, Sam and Sarah hugged his knees.

6
00:00:31.759 --> 00:00:35.648
"Don't be sad, Father," Sam said softly.

7
00:00:35.649 --> 00:00:40.297
"Tiny Tim would want us to be happy."

8
00:00:40.298 --> 00:00:44.464
Bob smiled at them, though his eyes were mournful.

9
00:00:44.465 --> 00:00:47.941
"I know Tiny Tim would want us to be cheerful.

10
00:00:47.942 --> 00:00:53.897
But it's difficult to feel happy when we miss him so much, isn't it?"

11
00:00:53.898 --> 00:01:00.370
His gaze wandered toward the tiny crutch that was leaning against the wall.

12
00:01:00.371 --> 00:01:03.525
"We'll go to church tomorrow for his funeral.

13
00:01:03.526 --> 00:01:11.395
After that, we'll just have to try to go on with life and be happy, as best as we can."

14
00:01:11.396 --> 00:01:18.652
His wife patted his hand. "Yes, we'll manage somehow."

15
00:01:18.653 --> 00:01:22.591
"Oh!" Cratchit sat up a little straighter.

16
00:01:22.592 --> 00:01:29.730
"I meant to tell you, dear, I met Mr. Scrooge's nephew, Fred, in the street today."

17
00:01:29.731 --> 00:01:35.028
"Did you?" His wife brushed a few tears from her eyes.

18
00:01:35.029 --> 00:01:40.843
"Yes. Fred remembered me and greeted me by name," Cratchit said.

19
00:01:40.844 --> 00:01:46.634
"I was quite impressed by his friendliness because we only met a few times.

20
00:01:46.635 --> 00:01:51.269
He even noticed that I looked unusually sad."

21
00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:56.438
"So unlike his uncle," Mrs. Cratchit murmured.

22
00:01:56.439 --> 00:02:00.596
Her husband nodded. "That's for sure.

23
00:02:00.597 --> 00:02:04.457
I told Fred the sad news about our Tim.

24
00:02:04.458 --> 00:02:11.964
He said, 'I am heartily sorry for it, Mr. Cratchit, and heartily sorry for your good wife.

25
00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:17.193
If I can be of help to you in any way, please come to me.'

26
00:02:17.194 --> 00:02:24.036
And then he gave me his card." Cratchit smiled weakly.

27
00:02:24.037 --> 00:02:29.805
"It truly seemed as if Fred had known Tiny Tim and missed him."

28
00:02:29.806 --> 00:02:32.510
Mrs. Cratchit looked down.

29
00:02:32.511 --> 00:02:38.317
"Nobody who knew Tiny Tim will ever forget him," she said softly.

30
00:02:38.318 --> 00:02:42.814
"No, never, Mother!" the children cried.

31
00:02:42.815 --> 00:02:48.731
"We must also remember how patient and mild Tim was," Cratchit said.

32
00:02:48.732 --> 00:02:54.131
"His example will remind us never to be unkind to others.

33
00:02:54.132 --> 00:02:57.470
Tiny Tim wouldn't like it." "No,

34
00:02:57.471 --> 00:03:03.124
never, Father!" the children said. Scrooge

35
00:03:03.125 --> 00:03:07.215
felt tears suddenly welling up in his eyes. He

36
00:03:07.216 --> 00:03:13.852
never could have imagined that so many people would feel such strong love for a young child. Then

37
00:03:13.853 --> 00:03:20.169
Scrooge remembered his sister, Fan, and the happy times they'd spent together as children. Fan

38
00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:25.089
had meant so much to him back then. Whoosh!

39
00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:32.371
The phantom startled him by waving its cloak over the whole scene. Now

40
00:03:32.372 --> 00:03:36.841
the Cratchits were standing together in a snowy churchyard. Martha

41
00:03:36.842 --> 00:03:41.482
was there, too, holding her mother's hand. Friends

42
00:03:41.483 --> 00:03:48.018
and neighbors stood nearby, and Fred was hurrying to join everyone. "I'm

43
00:03:48.019 --> 00:03:54.383
so sorry for your loss, Mr. and Mrs. Cratchit," Fred said, taking off his hat. "Thank

44
00:03:54.384 --> 00:03:59.593
you, sir," Bob Cratchit said, shaking Fred's hand. "We

45
00:03:59.594 --> 00:04:02.839
already miss Tiny Tim very much." "He

46
00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:06.674
was a wonderful boy," Fred said. Cratchit's

47
00:04:06.675 --> 00:04:13.800
eyes filled with tears. "He was indeed." Scrooge

48
00:04:13.801 --> 00:04:21.577
watched Tiny Tim's brothers and sisters move closer to Tiny Tim's grave, all holding hands. "I

49
00:04:21.578 --> 00:04:26.741
wish Tiny Tim could have lived another week, at least," Peter said. "He

50
00:04:26.742 --> 00:04:33.065
always loved Christmas. It doesn't seem fair that he has to miss it." "It

51
00:04:33.066 --> 00:04:37.560
doesn't seem fair at all!" Scrooge said. "I've

52
00:04:37.561 --> 00:04:45.439
seen enough, spirit. I've learned my lesson. Please take me home." The

53
00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:48.577
spirit didn't speak. But

54
00:04:48.578 --> 00:04:53.960
from the way it lifted its arm, Scrooge knew what it was telling him: "Not

55
00:04:53.961 --> 00:05:00.419
yet. There is more to see." Tiny

56
00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:06.512
Tim's funeral was gone, and now Scrooge was back in the heart of the bustling city. He

57
00:05:06.513 --> 00:05:11.475
looked around at the shops lining both sides of the street. ***

58
00:05:11.476 --> 00:05:15.832
"Why have you brought me here?" he asked the spirit.

59
00:05:15.833 --> 00:05:19.602
"It's not a place where I ever spent time."

60
00:05:19.603 --> 00:05:23.059
The spirit drifted toward a particular shop.

61
00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:28.259
Scrooge followed, squinting to make out the name on the sign out front.

62
00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:32.325
It was dusted with fresh snow.

63
00:05:32.326 --> 00:05:37.388
"Richard Wilkins, Tailor," he read aloud.

64
00:05:37.389 --> 00:05:42.600
"Oh! We're back to visit Dick Wilkins again.

65
00:05:42.601 --> 00:05:45.934
But I'm still quite confused, spirit.

66
00:05:45.935 --> 00:05:52.219
Are you saying that Wilkins is the only one who will miss me after I've died?"

67
00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:58.510
The spirit stared at Scrooge for a moment before beckoning him to follow.

68
00:05:58.511 --> 00:06:04.781
Together they entered the tailor's shop.

